## Decisions locked this session
- Project is UnityEve (D:\Projects\MindAttic\UnityEve), a Unity 6 survival-horror RPG vertical slice.
  Must-follow docs: AGENTS.md, docs/BIBLE.md. "Done" = tools/test.ps1 -Compile green + content rebuild
  + player build + `-autoplay` pass (0 FAIL lines) + screenshots reviewed.
- Owner explicitly directed (2026-10-11) growing beyond the original vertical slice into a fuller game:
  more districts, more enemies/moves, progression bones (keys/gates/puzzles), eventually plot/dialogue.
- Asset policy widened from CC0/OFL-only to also allow MIT (with attribution) — BIBLE.md UE-LAW-4 updated.
- Every model placement must go through `Model()`/`ConvertRenderers()` (scale + toon-shader re-skin) —
  this is now an ENFORCED build-time invariant (`DemoContentBuilder.ValidateMaterials()`, approved-shader
  allowlist), not just convention.
- Attribution for commits: `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` +
  `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kf5jJUX5aX7oj2Ckm2xUiW`.
- A "fork" subagent given explicit "research only" / "read-only, do not edit" instructions has TWICE
  this session gone ahead and written/fixed real files anyway (both times the result was actually good,
  but it's a reproducible instruction-following gap — already filed as feedback via SendFeedback, twice).
