## State / where we are
Everything through the Max Payne shootdodge feature is implemented, verified, committed, and pushed.
Latest commit: `05b21cd` "Ashgrove School, lock-and-key bones, a hand-aimed Line Rush, and a Max Payne
shootdodge (owner requests)" on `main`, pushed to `origin/main` (previous commit was `e7a7510`).

Full list of what shipped in that commit (all verified via dotnet test 66/66, Unity compile clean,
content rebuild clean incl. the new material-conversion check, Windows build, `-autoplay` PASS 0 FAIL):
- **Ashgrove School** district (DemoContentBuilder.School.cs, new) with two new alien enemies: Bloat
  Spitter (ranged, leaves a DOT acid puddle — HazardPuddle.cs, new) and Husk Warden (tanky blocker).
- **Lock-and-key "bones"**: Core/Story/LockGraph.cs (new, pure C#, 5 unit tests) — a solvability
  fixpoint-reachability checker wired into `DemoContentBuilder.BuildAll()` via `ValidateLocks()`, so any
  future door/gate whose key becomes unreachable fails the content build loudly. Runtime/Interaction/
  Gate.cs (new) — an in-place locked barrier (vs. Door's scene-transition), with save/load support
  (SaveGame.UnlockedGates / SaveSystem.cs).
- **Combat moves**: Shove (free melee, Interact in battle), Riposte (upgraded Focus "Counter" — full
  damage, guaranteed crit), Line Rush (BattlePhase.Aiming — hand-rotated straight-line dash/cut,
  BladeArts.AimedRushEnd, kept alongside the original lock-on Rush per explicit owner instruction
  "keep both"), and the new **Shootdodge** (Max Payne dive: leap in chosen direction, bullet time via
  WorldTime.SetScale, fire at nearest enemy per Confirm press while airborne spending real ammo, hard
  landing = flat self-damage + root/stun). Wasp retrofitted to Ranged (dodgeable sting, no puddle).
- **Container rummaging**: multi-stage "Rummaging..." (up to 3 stages, Container.MaxStages), a glint
  marking unsearched containers (amber, vs Pickup's cyan).
- **Car-kit assets**: Kenney Car Kit (CC0) added at Art/Models/car-kit/ — sedan, taxi, suv, etc. placed
  around town (careful placement to avoid lamp-post/other-prop overlaps — see bugs below).
- **Bug-hunt pass** (user asked "find and fix bugs", used the `/bughunt` skill): unbounded search via
  4 parallel read-only forks + my own review, found and fixed 7 real bugs: Container re-roll-past-cap
  exploit, BattlePhase.Aiming GameObject/HUD-prompt leak on Victory/Defeat, Shove/Riposte knockback
  missing arena clamp (KeepInArena), ObstacleAwareness picking wrong (non-directional) obstacle,
  HazardPuddle's first DOT tick firing instantly on spawn, a duplicate car overlapping a pre-existing
  procedural car at the Heights parking lot, and the new cars being under-scaled (~half size of every
  other vehicle) — all fixed, all re-verified.
- Input: new `ShootdodgePressed` binding (gamepad right shoulder / keyboard Left Ctrl), with a
  `TriggerShootdodge()` scripted-input override for the autopilot (mirrors TriggerDodge/TriggerConfirm).
- Autopilot.cs exercises Line Rush (turn==4) and Shootdodge (turn==6) explicitly for `-autoplay` coverage
  — confirmed working via screenshots (e.g. `107_encounter_5_square_shootdodge.png` /
  `..._shootdodge_land.png`, also fired once during the boss fight).

